        "text": "Unlike other hindu temples, the architecture of Pasupathinath Temple is like a pagoda temple.\nThe shrine is also very different from other shivlingas. The first thing you notice while entering the shrine is a mighty golden statue of a bull or Nandi. Behind the statue of Nandi, is the four headed Shiv Ling.\nThere are other temples of Ganesha, Bhairavnath, Durga, Narayana with in the shrine.\nI did not expect that burning rituals are also done within the same premises by the side of baghmati river.\nOverall it is a divine experience.",
