        "title": "Shivaratri festival. P",
        "text": "Fascinating is the only way I can describe my experience last Thursday the 27 th. Feb.  so many Sadhus smoking pot ( illegal but allowed for the festival).  Hindus making puja to the gods in the shrines and temples and then down to the river to watch the goings on, listen to music, wander among the sadhus and get their blessings if willing to pay.  Not being a Hindu we could not enter the temple of Shiva but we were able to wander around the many shrines.  We came in from the back, across the river from the temple and went in the morning when the crowds were not bad.  Returning early afternoon was frightening, with crowds pushing both ways up the stairs.  A friend went in the evening and there were huge crowds then too.\nWe also saw a cremation as they take place on the river near the temple.",
