        "title": "Ancient temple and crematorium",
        "text": "i went to this place with a tourist guide who explained me in details all about the temple. At a first glance it was not really interesting for me because is not really well preserved, however after understand how old is it and the meaning of it my perception changed completely. I was able to observe the cremation and the ceremony before it. Next to the place an hospital is located where patients in palliative care are sent to be closer to the holly river.\nThere is a toilet facility (not really good) exclusively for tourist. The entrance fee is quite expensive for Nepal (1000 NR) but is a must see place in Kathmandu.",
